# Data conversion between gibibyte and kilobyte

Verifies direct data conversion between gibibyte and kilobyte in both directions. Forward, converting 1GiB to 1073741.824KB with a fractional coarser-to-finer scale promotes the integer result to decimal, while 1.5GiB yields 1610612.736KB; backward, converting 1KB to 0.0000GiB with a fractional finer-to-coarser scale promotes the integer result to decimal, while 1.5KB yields 0.0000GiB. Tiny magnitudes round to four fractional digits.

>>> source
forward_whole: int = 1GiB
print(forward_whole->to(KB))
forward_fractional: decimal = 1.5GiB
print(forward_fractional->to(KB))
backward_whole: int = 1KB
print(backward_whole->to(GiB))
backward_fractional: decimal = 1.5KB
print(backward_fractional->to(GiB))

<<< stdout
1073741.824KB
1610612.736KB
0.0000GiB
0.0000GiB

<<< stderr
